1260	// The condense is fail-open. Doctor retries no-files ENDED sessions; an error
1261	// marking the session ended is returned so callers can react, and skips the
1262	// condense since the state may be inconsistent. event may be nil when no hook
1263	// event drives the end (the sweep), which skips event-metadata persistence.
1264	// guard is forwarded to markSessionEnded (see there); when it skips the end,
1265	// the condense is skipped too and ended is false.
1266	//
1267	// condenseDeadline, when non-zero, bounds only the condense — never the
1268	// mark-ended write, so the cheap step that un-sticks the session from `entire
1269	// status` is never the one given up on. The bound is best-effort: it cancels git
1270	// subprocesses and any context-aware step, but condensation does not poll ctx
1271	// between stages, so it curtails rather than guarantees. Its purpose is to stop
1272	// short of a host that kills the hook's whole process tree (Codex) rather than
1273	// to make condensation interruptible.
1274	//
1275	// Leaving mark-ended unbounded is not the same as guaranteeing it. It runs under
1276	// MutateSessionState, whose flock acquire blocks (WithSessionLockWait is opt-in,
1277	// and only TurnStart opts in), so a concurrent turn-end condense holding the
1278	// same per-session lock can push it past the host's cap and get the whole tree
1279	// killed. The exited-owner sweep is the backstop for that: the session is
